From fa1252223c1281141a4f79c7fe58f45609a43d46 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: titanism <101466223+titanism@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 21:49:13 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] fix: detection, false positives, hostile input, servers and
 packaging

Links and text
- links: keep a link's userinfo, read links at the end of a line, cell or
  block, bracketed and entity-split links, every link in the message up to
  phishing.maxLength (linksTruncated past it), exec loops instead of
  matchAll (RE2 recompiled each call); hosts outside [a-z0-9_-] handled
- deceptive links: the whole text, or an http(s) address inside it; no
  file names, versions or site names in prose; through click tracking only
  a brand's home or sign-in address from a sender that is not the brand or
  one of its sending domains (scan() now passes the From domain)
- links unwrapped from Safe Links, Proofpoint and click trackers for
  lookups and lookalike checks; links in the shown text of HTML read too,
  broken where a browser breaks the line (blocks, cells, styled blocks)
- html: visible text as browsers build it (foster parenting, templates,
  svg/math, formatting reopened, quirks), hidden text, entity prefixes
  in linear time (formatting reopened 12 deep, styles read once); tag
  names like <constructor> no longer crash it
- obfuscation: bidi overrides always count, letter-digit invisibles count,
  unit letters only in units; HTML text counts beside a plain part
- homograph: fewer false positives on words and short brands; word brands
  beside service or product words, sign-in labels, rn/cl/vv/l-for-i swaps
- rules: FROM_NAME_BRAND with official and sending domains listed (not
  brand+mail patterns), joined names only as the display name says them,
  linear in the display name; Apple names by the word next to it (one
  filler allowed, other businesses and shops named with a place not); a
  display name that is a brand's
  address (not a shared registry such as gov.uk); SEXTORTION_SUBJECT and
  hacked-account subjects 6 only with a real payment demand (amounts in
  many currencies and wordings; an amount alone only with a threat, and
  "everyone will see" only of the recording itself);
  TYPO_DOMAIN for dropped or doubled letters (twiter, samsng);
  PROMPT_INJECTION in HTML attributes and with a verdict claim after
  "ignore the previous instructions", only as instructions about this
  message's verdict, not in a form's help text; PAYPAL_INVOICE and other rule wording tightened;
  RISKY_ATTACHMENT_TYPE, SCRIPT_IN_ARCHIVE

Parsing and scanning
- src/parse.js: mailparser without html-to-text (quadratic on deep HTML);
  every message finished so mailparser never hangs on one ending in an
  attached message's header; past its limits (1000 parts, 1 MB header) a
  message is read as far as it can be (oversized headers cut down so From
  survives) and gets MIME_TOO_COMPLEX, which no credit offsets; attached
  messages (message/rfc822, .eml) opened 3 levels deep, 100 attachments,
  never failing the scan
- ClamAV: four at a time within its own clamav.timeout (60 s); errors in
  results.virusScanErrors, files over StreamMaxLength in virusScanSkipped;
  host/port of the clamscan option read
- allowlist: From only when authenticated (DMARC for its organizational
  domain, or a passing aligned DKIM signature by registrable domain; a
  subdomain entry only from that domain, under it or a parent; never a
  domain that is not a hostname, a public suffix, or results without their
  domain); IDN and punycode match; reputation caches shared per service
- authentication: a DKIM signature with l= shorter than the body earns
  no credit or trust; DMARC policy and strict alignment read from the
  record and enforced; DMARC fails without exactly one From address;
  DMARC_FAIL small for p=none with SPF counted on top; ARC trusted only
  when the newest set is sealed by a trusted domain and vouches for From,
  and then no SELF_SPOOF
- denylist matches any name under a listed domain, bounded; IPv6 entries
  and clients in RFC 5952 form; SURBL/Spamhaus error answers not listings
- allowedLanguages reads no, fil, iw, in and ji; Russian, Bulgarian and
  other Slavic text with a Kazakh name or word keeps its language
- per-scan options merged with the scanner's, undefined keeps defaults;
  timeouts for authentication, NSFW and network checks; timedOutHosts
- classifier: models validated on load, null options of 7.0.3 read as
  meant; saveModel atomic and tidy; typedefs and dist types (.d.cts,
  legacy options) match the code

Language model
- verdicts only from the answer, never from reasoning that quotes the
  message (think spans, orphan close tags, unclosed reasoning), denials
  incl. curly apostrophes, negated labels, minimum verdict mass; more
  denials ("unlikely to be", "not considered", "neither ... nor", verdict
  words joined to a denied one); notspam/nonspam labels
- request slots by deadline, shared in-flight requests, no request with
  too little time left; local presets keep their asking method on another
  machine but redact mail sent outside a private network; one-line fields

Servers and CLI
- milter: packet reassembly, 1 MB packet limit, tempfail (or marked
  accept with onError / --on-error accept) for failed scans and
  attachments ClamAV could not scan; X-Spam-Virus-Scan: failed; sender
  X-Spam headers removed; listener errors reported
- subject tags: non-ASCII or "=?" text RFC 2047-encoded in words of at
  most 75 characters, folded within line limits, the space before the
  subject kept, control characters removed, nothing added for an empty
  tag; headers added at the top of a message with no header block
- filter exits 75 for unscanned mail unless --on-error accept; spamd and
  TCP idle timeouts, protocol limits, half-open connections closed
- ARF: bounded address search, quoted-printable into a Buffer, create()
  with RFC 2047 subjects, validated dates and Buffer in/out

Packaging, docs and tests
- release: install.sh attached at once, SHA256SUMS after every build,
  checksums verified by install.sh; train-model pins and checks datasets
- docs and all 24 translations updated; tests for every fix, no network,
  no fixed ports, timing in processor time, 100% coverage
